 112:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** /*
 113:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** The 433.92 Mhz receivers have AGC, if no signal is present the gain will be set
 114:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** to its highest level.
 115:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** 
 116:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** In this condition it will switch high to low at random intervals due to input noise.
 117:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** A CRO connected to the data line looks like 433.92 is full of transmissions.
 118:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** 
 119:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** Any ASK transmission method must first sent a capture signal of 101010........
 120:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** When the receiver has adjusted its AGC to the required level for the transmisssion
 121:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** the actual data transmission can occur.
 122:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** 
 123:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** We send 14 0's 1010... It takes 1 to 3 10's for the receiver to adjust to
 124:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** the transmit level.
 125:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** 
 126:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** The receiver waits until we have at least 10 10's and then a start pulse 01.
 127:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** The receiver is then operating correctly and we have locked onto the transmission.
 128:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** */
